{"id": 10, "ts": 1780638764.3983219, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fA\u2019s technical and decision\u2011making strengths, but the new data on the other candidates forces us to reassess the overall fit, especially regarding crew cooperation and stress resilience\u2014key for long\u2011distance operations. Candidate\u202fB handles stress very well, yet is uncooperative and can be grumpy, which raises serious concerns about cockpit harmony. Candidate\u202fC, while creating a positive crew atmosphere, struggles to communicate ideas and is seen as egocentric, undermining professional communication. Candidate\u202fD responds adequately to unexpected events but is perceived as arrogant with weak leadership, also problematic for crew dynamics. Compared with these, Candidate\u202fA\u2019s interpersonal drawbacks (unfriendly, show\u2011off attitude) are still concerning, but they appear less detrimental than the clear cooperation and communication deficits of B, C, and D. Therefore, I continue to support Candidate\u202fA as the provisional recommendation, while urging that we probe his willingness to accept feedback and address his unfriendly demeanor before final hiring."}
