{"id": 22, "ts": 1780638863.6269279, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fA is our best overall fit, even though we still lack concrete evidence of his stress\u2011resilience on prolonged flights. The strengths we have\u2014anticipating dangerous situations, seeing complex connections, excellent spatial vision, and very good leadership\u2014directly support operational reliability, technical competence, decision quality, and responsibility, which are critical for long\u2011distance operations. While his unfriendly demeanor, occasional resistance to criticism, and unorganized habits are concerns, they appear less detrimental than the clear crew\u2011cooperation and communication deficits we see in Candidates\u202fB,\u202fC, and\u202fD (e.g., B\u2019s uncooperative, grumpy attitude; C\u2019s egocentric communication style; D\u2019s arrogance and weak leadership). Therefore, I continue to provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fA, with the condition that we further probe his ability to handle sustained stress and his openness to feedback before finalizing the hire."}
